    title: "Plato's cave: what does an allegory told for two thousand years actually say?",
    slug: "platos-allegory-of-the-cave",
    summary:
      "The allegory of the cave in Book VII of the Republic sets out the difference between knowledge and appearance. Why it is invoked so often in arguments about screens, algorithms and information.",
    coverImage: "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Plato_Silanion_Musei_Capitolini_MC1377.jpg?width=1600",
    imageCredit: "Bust of Plato, Musei Capitolini · Wikimedia Commons",
    featured: false,
    sourceName: null,
