    title: "This Day in Philosophy — 22 August: the Haitian uprising and the first Geneva Convention",
    slug: "haiti-uprising-first-geneva-convention",
    summary: "The uprising that began at Saint-Domingue on 22 August 1791 became the hardest test the universality of human rights has faced. On the same day in 1864 the first Geneva Convention was signed, committing to paper the idea that even war has limits.",
