    title: "Homo pictor: Art, Imagination and Creation",
    slug: "shaf-homo-pictor-congress-barcelona-2026",
    summary:
      "The 16th International Congress of the Hispanic Society of Philosophical Anthropology, held at UIC Barcelona, takes as its theme Hans Jonas's figure of the human being as the image-making animal, and asks what artistic creation means under artificial intelligence and ecological pressure.",
    description: `The Sociedad Hispanica de Antropologia Filosofica (SHAF) holds its sixteenth international congress at the Universitat Internacional de Catalunya from 30 September to 2 October 2026, on the theme *Homo pictor: Art, Imagination and Creation*.

The phrase is Hans Jonas's, from his 1961 essay "Homo pictor und die differentia des Menschen": the proposal that what marks the human off from other animals is not tool use but the capacity to make and recognise images. The congress asks what remains of that claim now that image-making has been automated, and how creation, imagination and skill should be understood under new technologies and the ecological crisis.

Fifteen thematic lines are set out in the call for papers, seven general and eight specific. The general lines cover the history of philosophical anthropology; anthropology, phenomenology and hermeneutics; art, cinema and literature; feminist philosophy; culture and religion; applied philosophy; and Spanish and Ibero-American philosophy. The specific lines run from the anthropological roots of artistic activity through art and health, art and the ecological crisis, gesture and expressivity, symbolism and transcendence, image and imaginary, to the obsolescence of creativity and new technologies.

Papers were accepted in Spanish and the other languages of Spain, and in English, French, Italian and Portuguese. Abstracts closed on 15 May 2026 and registration ran from 15 June to 15 July.

Organising committee: Xavier Escribano, Andrea Rodriguez Prat and Albert Moya (UIC Barcelona), Juan Velazquez (Zaragoza) and Noe Exposito Ropero (UNED).`,
