    description: `The London Centre for Interdisciplinary Research holds "Beyond Labels": International Conference on Disability, Different Ability and Neurodiversity at Birkbeck, University of London, on 12 and 13 September 2026.

The conference examines the shifting narratives, representations and lived experiences surrounding ability and difference. Topics in the call include disability as a social construct, representation in the media and the arts, neurodiversity in education, the intersections of disability with race and gender, assistive technologies, and disability and human rights.

The meeting is deliberately interdisciplinary: philosophers appear alongside sociologists, educationists, legal scholars, artists and practitioners, and papers arguing from lived experience are explicitly welcomed. For philosophers the natural points of entry are the metaphysics of impairment and disability, the epistemology of testimony and self-report, and the well-being and capability literatures.

Participation is hybrid. Presenters in London pay £150 and online presenters £90. Proposals of up to 250 words, with a short biographical note, closed on 25 May 2026.`,
